            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the German for to employ, then the German for fixed-term."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: die Teilzeit",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "die Teilzeit — \"part-time (work)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Seit der Geburt ihres Sohnes arbeitet sie in Teilzeit. Since the birth of her son she has been working part-time."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In Teilzeit arbeiten or Teilzeit arbeiten. Der Teilzeitjob — the part-time job."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Teilzeit joins Teil \"part\", Old High German teil, Proto-Germanic dailą (EtymDB), to Zeit \"time\", Old High German zīt, Proto-Germanic tīdiz (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
