          "title": "You'll want to know: die Schicht",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "die Schicht — \"the shift (at work); the layer\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ihre Schicht beginnt um sechs Uhr morgens. Her shift starts at six in the morning."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: die Schichten. Die Nachtschicht — the night shift. Also a layer: eine Schicht Schnee."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Schicht is usually traced to Middle Low German schicht, a word of the mines for a layer of rock and for a stint of work. EtymDB gives no history for it, but lists English shift as a cousin."
            }
          ]
        },
