          "title": "You'll want to know: der Feierabend",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "der Feierabend — \"the end of the working day; the evening off\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Nach Feierabend gehe ich gern schwimmen. After work I like to go swimming."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feierabend machen — to finish work for the day. Schönen Feierabend! — Enjoy your evening!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feierabend joins Feier, from Old High German fīra and Latin fēriae \"holidays\" (EtymDB; Lewis & Short), to Abend \"evening\", inherited from Old High German āband (EtymDB). It is usually said to have first meant the evening before a holiday."
            }
          ]
        },
